# Must-fix before claiming performance

When improving this project, prioritize closing these gaps **before** claiming top-retail or high-performance results. Do not treat P&L targets, Sharpe goals, or “edge proven” language as met until P0–P1 below are real in code and evidence.

This backlog is the single source of priority truth. It is read fresh (not cached) and checked against actual code each run by the **`Guruji_for_Bhale_Bullodu`** skill (`.claude/skills/Guruji_for_Bhale_Bullodu/`), which reports each item below as Done / Partial / Not-done with file/line evidence and keeps an open/resolved backlog. Editing this file changes what Guruji checks on its very next run — there is no separate copy to keep in sync.

## P0 — integrity of the trading loop

1. **Wire recommend → supervised approve → `paper_sim` → learning**
   One ledger must be the source of truth. Recommendations must not “fill” outside `paper_sim`; approve/reject must be real backend APIs when `SUPERVISION_MODE=supervised`.
   - **Definition of done:** `decisions` router exposes real `POST /approve` and `POST /reject` transitions (not read-only list/get endpoints); every accepted decision writes through to the `paper_sim` ledger and no other path can create a "filled" position; `/learning` outcomes are derived only from real ledger closes, with zero `"seed": true` / demo records mixed into the metrics used for reporting.

2. **Enforce breakers + market hours + durable positions**
   Daily-loss / circuit-breaker / session-window checks must reject or pause submit paths (not dashboard-only). Open book must survive process restart.
   - **Definition of done:** the open-position book is persisted (file/DB), not in-memory process globals; a killed/restarted process resumes with the same open positions it had before the restart; daily-loss, circuit-breaker, and market-hours/session-window checks run inside the actual submit path (paper_sim engine and any live broker path), verified by grep/trace, not only surfaced as dashboard metrics.

## P1 — proof of edge

3. **Options-chain walk-forward / replay for SH-4 expectancy**
   No “top performing” claims without OOS options PnL evidence for the long-vol playbook.
   - **Definition of done:** a checked-in walk-forward or replay artifact (script + result output) exists that runs the SH-4 playbook against historical options-chain data with an explicit train/test (in-sample vs. out-of-sample) split, and reports expectancy/PnL on the OOS slice specifically — not just backtested-in-sample numbers.

4. **Skew / term / India VIX regime filters + better IV**
   Surface-aware filters and proper IV quality before treating signals as institutional-grade retail vol.
   - **Definition of done:** an identifiable module (e.g. under `backend/quant`) computes skew and term-structure signals and gates or adjusts strategy selection using them, in addition to the existing India VIX level wiring; IV inputs used by signals have a documented quality/sanity check (not raw passthrough of a single broker mark).

## P2 — tradeable quality & live safety

5. **Structure sizing** (delta/vega targets, lots, costs) — turn signals into expectancy after costs.
   - **Definition of done:** position sizing derives lot count from explicit delta/vega targets and includes brokerage/slippage/margin costs in the expectancy calculation shown to the operator or used in ranking — not a flat/arbitrary lot size.
6. **Fill / reconcile FSM** before any live micro-capital (Phase 5).
   - **Definition of done:** an explicit fill/reconcile state machine (submitted → partial → filled/rejected → reconciled) exists and is tested, so a live order's true state is always derivable and never silently assumed.

## Guidance for agents

- Prefer work that closes P0 over net-new strategy/UI features when the user asks for performance, readiness, or “make it better.”
- If proposing a roadmap, keep this order unless the user explicitly overrides it.
- Never imply the vol edge is validated without walk-forward / OOS evidence (P1 item 3).
- Any item marked Partial or Not-done by Guruji stays open in `Docs/bot_health/BACKLOG.md` until its Definition of Done is met with cited evidence — not until it merely looks addressed.
